Parts of the native runtime are derived from AOSP sources and interface
definitions — the libgui/SurfaceFlinger C++ shims, the binder/AIDL bindings, and
the vendored `.aidl` interfaces they are generated from. The AOSP trees
themselves are consumed as submodules and retain their own copyright headers.

